2. **Citation Content (References to Prior Work)**:
   - The phrase *"Due to space limitations, these experiments and the details of our synthetic datasets are provided in the technical report [14]"* explicitly references a prior work (their own technical report, cited as [14]). 
   - **Why it's high**: This is a clear citation to a prior work (even if it is the authors' own previous report), which falls under "citation content" as it serves to direct readers to supplementary material. In academic contexts, such references are standard for managing space constraints and are not considered technical contributions. This portion constitutes ≈80% of the text.

